# A release checklist where each item is a job whose goal says what done means, and
# `ls jobs` is the board. One item verifies; the other comes back unfinished, and wait
# says which goal is unmet, repeats the risk its holder reported, and sends it back to rework.
# docs/guides/jobs/other-work.md shows these commands and every golden below verbatim
# (TestJobGuideMatchesItsScripts holds it to that).
env HOME=$WORK/home
env XDG_STATE_HOME=$WORK/home/state
env GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=Ana
env GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=ana@example.com
env GIT_COMMITTER_NAME=Ana
env GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL=ana@example.com
env GIT_AUTHOR_DATE=2026-10-01T09:00:00Z
env GIT_COMMITTER_DATE=2026-10-01T09:00:00Z
cd shop
exec git init -q -b main
exec git add -A
exec git commit -q -m 'ready to cut 1.3'

stdin $WORK/checklist.jsonl
exec magus job apply --stdin
cmp stdout $WORK/apply.out
exec git worktree add -q ../changelog
exec git worktree add -q ../notes

cd ../changelog
exec magus job exec release-1.3/changelog
cp $WORK/CHANGELOG.md CHANGELOG.md
exec git commit -q -am 'add 1.3 changelog entry'
stdin $WORK/changelog.json
exec magus job exit release-1.3/changelog --stdin

cd ../notes
exec magus job exec release-1.3/notes
stdin $WORK/notes.json
exec magus job exit release-1.3/notes --stdin
cmp stdout $WORK/exit-notes.out

cd ../shop
exec magus ls jobs
cp stdout $WORK/raw
exec sh -c 'sed -e "s|$WORK|~/src|g" "$WORK/raw"'
cmp stdout $WORK/ls-exited.out
exec magus job wait release-1.3/changelog
cmp stdout $WORK/wait-changelog.out
! exec magus job wait release-1.3/notes
cmp stdout $WORK/wait-notes.out
exec magus ls jobs --all
cp stdout $WORK/raw
exec sh -c 'sed -e "s|$WORK|~/src|g" "$WORK/raw"'
cmp stdout $WORK/ls-board.out

-- shop/.gitignore --
.magus/
-- shop/magus.yaml --
concurrency: 2
-- shop/magusfile.buzz --
import "magus";
-- shop/CHANGELOG.md --
# Changelog

## 1.2
-- CHANGELOG.md --
# Changelog

## 1.3

- Prices are computed in cents.

## 1.2
-- checklist.jsonl --
{"api_version": "magus.job/v1alpha1", "id": "release-1.3/changelog", "model": "standard", "criteria": "CHANGELOG.md has a 1.3 section", "write_paths": ["CHANGELOG.md"], "goals": [{"id": "changelog", "kind": "paths", "expect": "changed", "paths": ["CHANGELOG.md"]}]}
{"api_version": "magus.job/v1alpha1", "id": "release-1.3/notes", "model": "standard", "criteria": "release notes exist for 1.3", "write_paths": ["notes/1.3.md"], "goals": [{"id": "notes", "kind": "paths", "expect": "present", "paths": ["notes/1.3.md"]}]}
-- changelog.json --
{"api_version": "magus.job-result/v1alpha1", "changed_paths": ["CHANGELOG.md"], "unresolved_risks": []}
-- notes.json --
{"api_version": "magus.job-result/v1alpha1", "changed_paths": [], "unresolved_risks": ["the notes need the final benchmark numbers"]}
-- apply.out --
created release-1.3/changelog, declared, with 1 write path(s)
model tier: standard (rank 1), row: "the job names the tier standard"
created release-1.3/notes, declared, with 1 write path(s)
model tier: standard (rank 1), row: "the job names the tier standard"
-- exit-notes.out --
exited release-1.3/notes, recorded exited, with its result filed. Whoever forked it verifies with `magus job wait release-1.3/notes`
-- ls-exited.out --
JOB                    HOLDER     STATE   MODEL     PATHS  PROOF     CHECK
release-1.3/changelog  changelog  exited  standard  1      alone     -
release-1.3/notes      notes      exited  standard  1      disjoint  -

not merged onto main: 1
  release-1.3/changelog at 7b9e9dc: 1 commit(s) at 7b9e9dc are not on main; merge 7b9e9dc into main, or state why it stays off: `magus job apply --stdin` with {"api_version":"magus.job/v1alpha1","id":"release-1.3/changelog","left_unmerged":"<why>"}
unresolved risks, which stop nothing: 1
  release-1.3/notes: "the notes need the final benchmark numbers"
in flight: never fetched; `magus queue ls --provider <provider> --base <branch>` reads the open changes
-- wait-changelog.out --
verified release-1.3/changelog, recorded pass
goal changelog: verified
footprint: where its diff since the checkpoint landed
  CHANGELOG.md:3-6
-- wait-notes.out --
rejected release-1.3/notes
  job release-1.3/notes is not read-only and the result claims no changed paths at all
  nothing in the diff since 5f6b136f2721af3fb8a117fbf824b24a3a78b059 is inside its write paths (notes/1.3.md)
  goal "notes": nothing matching "notes/1.3.md" is in the tree, so this goal is unmet
release-1.3/notes is running again and holds its write paths again for its rework
goal notes: rejected
footprint: no line changed since the checkpoint
unresolved risks its holder reported
  the notes need the final benchmark numbers
-- ls-board.out --
JOB                    HOLDER     STATE    MODEL     PATHS  PROOF     CHECK
release-1.3/changelog  changelog  pass     standard  1      alone     -
release-1.3/notes      notes      running  standard  1      disjoint  -

not merged onto main: 1
  release-1.3/changelog at 7b9e9dc: 1 commit(s) at 7b9e9dc are not on main; merge 7b9e9dc into main, or state why it stays off: `magus job apply --stdin` with {"api_version":"magus.job/v1alpha1","id":"release-1.3/changelog","left_unmerged":"<why>"}
unresolved risks, which stop nothing: 1
  release-1.3/notes: "the notes need the final benchmark numbers"
in flight: never fetched; `magus queue ls --provider <provider> --base <branch>` reads the open changes
